4. No software charges or paid installation

You may not:

a. Sell, rent or charge for copies, licenses, downloads, updates or access to
   the Software, including modified versions.
b. Require payment for activation, feature unlocks, subscriptions, premium
   editions or exclusive or early access to the Software or its features.
c. Include the Software in a paid software product or paid software bundle.
d. Charge others for installing, setting up, configuring or deploying the
   Software, including where the Software itself is described as free.
e. Make payment for another item or service a condition of receiving,
   accessing, using or installing the Software.

These restrictions apply to direct and indirect charges and to required
non-monetary compensation.

Free redistribution and free installation assistance are permitted.

Genuinely voluntary donations are permitted only if they are not required to
receive, access, use or install the Software and do not purchase exclusive or
early software access, features or installation services.

This license provides no written-permission exception to these restrictions.

5. Distribution and corresponding source

Every distributed copy or modified version must include this license and
preserve applicable copyright, attribution and third-party notices.

Modifications must be clearly identified. Modified versions must not falsely
claim official status or endorsement.

When distributing the Software in binary or another non-source form, you must
provide each recipient, without charge, with its complete corresponding source
under this license.

"Complete corresponding source" means the preferred form for modifying the
covered Software, including the changes, project build scripts, dependency
information and instructions reasonably necessary to build that version.

For a public distribution, the corresponding source must be publicly
downloadable without charge no later than the binary release. A release tag or
commit and its source archive must identify the exact version used. Source for
a different version does not satisfy this requirement.

If the source is provided through a download link, it must remain available for
at least three years after your last distribution of that version.

You may not impose additional terms that prevent recipients from exercising
the rights granted by this license.

Private development and testing do not by themselves require public release.
Privately distributed binaries must nevertheless be accompanied by
corresponding source for their recipients.

Separately licensed third-party components, general-purpose development tools
and vendor firmware are excluded from this source requirement to the extent
they are not covered by this license. Necessary dependencies must be
identified, together with their applicable licenses and lawful acquisition
instructions. This exclusion does not permit withholding covered project
source or modifications.

